This is a known breaking change. .NET 10 MAUI adopts Android 15's **edge-to-edge** mode by default, which means `adjustResize` no longer automatically shrinks your layout. You now need to respond to **IME window insets**.

**Recommended fix — handle insets via platform code:**

In your `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Compatibility.Platform.Android;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        // Still needed — tells Android to resize content area
        Window!.SetSoftInputMode(SoftInput.AdjustResize);

        // React to IME (keyboard) insets under edge-to-edge
        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(
            Window.DecorView.FindViewById(Android.Resource.Id.Content)!,
            new KeyboardInsetsListener());
    }

    class KeyboardInsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View view, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var systemBarInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

            // Use the larger of IME or nav-bar bottom inset
            int bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBarInsets.Bottom);
            view.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottomPadding);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

**What changed & why:**
| .NET 9 | .NET 10 |
|---|---|
| `adjustResize` shrinks the window | Edge-to-edge draws behind system bars; `adjustResize` only reports insets |
| `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` handled it | You must consume `Ime()` insets yourself |

**iOS** is unaffected — MAUI's `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` still handles it. If you need to disable/tweak it:

```csharp
// MauiProgram.cs
builder.ConfigureMauiHandlers(h =>
{
    Microsoft.Maui.Platform.KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect();
});
```

This approach gives you full control over how the layout adjusts when the keyboard appears.
